  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 235 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nThe predominant westerly flow aloft will keep the surface boundary \nin the vicinity of Iowa through much of next week. This will have a \ncouple impacts. First the wildfire smoke listed above will persist \nat times. In addition, the active weather pattern will persist with \nperiodic chances for thunderstorms. The storms will bring an \nattendant chance for severe weather and the potential for heavy \nrainfall. At this time, it appears that dryer air and Canadian High \npressure may bring a brief reprieve of the active and humid weather \nbut already there are hints that return flow and active weather \ncould again return again sometime next weekend.",
